===================================================================
 SMART LAB DOOR - PIPELINE SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE & THREADING FLOW
===================================================================

[START: main.py]
       |
       v
[INITIALIZE: app.py] 
  1. Load Face database from SQLite (smart_door.db)
  2. Sync user names and 512-dim embeddings to binary cache (scratch/db.bin)
  3. Start GStreamer pipeline thread & UI / Event loops
       |
       +---------------------------------------------------------------+
       |                                                               |
[THREAD 1: AUTO RE-SYNC / RELOAD]                         [THREAD 2: LIVE GSTREAMER NPU PIPELINE]
(Runs in background in Python)                             (Driven by GStreamer C-Core & NPU)
       |                                                               |
       v                                                               v
1. Monitor SQLite database mtime.                          1. Read camera frame (v4l2src).
2. On change, reload known users in Python.                2. Run YOLOv8-Face (yolo26_landmark.hef).
3. Re-serialize embeddings to binary (db.bin).             3. Run YOLO Post-proc (libyolo26_landmark_post.so).
4. Signal C++ DB Matcher to hot-reload db.bin.            4. Run Box Tracking (hailotracker).
                                                           5. Crop face ROIs (hailocropper / all_detections).
                                                           6. Run Face embedding (arcface_mobilefacenet.hef).
                                                           7. Extract 512-dim embedding (libarcface_post.so).
                                                           8. Sync crops back to main frame (hailoaggregator).
                                                           9. Run C++ DB matcher (libdb_matcher_post.so)
                                                              - Match embedding using vector dot products.
                                                              - Attach recognition classification metadata.
                                                              - Remove matrix to prevent tracker propagation.
                                                          10. Send frame to output (fakesink).
                                                              |
                                                              v
                                                   [PYTHON PAD PROBE (fakesink)]
                                                      - Maps GStreamer buffer via ctypes.
                                                      - Wraps buffer in a zero-copy numpy array.
                                                      - Draws modern Sci-fi style overlays:
                                                         * Green corner bounding boxes (Known)
                                                         * Red corner bounding boxes (Unknown)
                                                         * Face landmarks (magenta dots)
                                                         * Name and similarity percent text
                                                      - Pushes updates to controller / DB.
